NAME: Credit watch
OWNER: Revenue Partner
ROLE: revenue-partner
WHEN: Every day at 12:41 PM NZ time (The CRON line is UTC, like your existing jobs. NZ daylight time shown; in NZ winter it runs an hour earlier by the NZ clock.)
CRON: 41 23 * * *
CRON_NZ: 41 12 * * *
SKILLS: scdt-credit-watch
STATUS: Created paused. Turned on only after Jesse says yes.
---
Stop check: if ~/.hermes/scdt/state/EXTERNAL_WRITES_STOPPED exists, read only, send nothing to anyone but Jesse, report the recorded reason, and stop.
Times are Pacific/Auckland. Every number names its source and read time. Nothing goes to anyone but Jesse without his exact reply words for that item (scdt-business-context, "Sending an email"), unless ~/.hermes/scdt/context/standing-approvals.md covers that exact message.
Run log: when you finish, append "<time> · Credit watch · EXECUTED · <one-line result>" to ~/.hermes/scdt/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md, or NO_CHANGE, or FAILED with the reason. A source you couldn't read is UNKNOWN, never zero.
Cost: One tiny run a day: one web request, no drafting. Leave it paused for good if this agent already warns about low credit (see the skill).

The job: follow scdt-credit-watch, "Each run".
1. Read the remaining OpenRouter credit (never print the key).
2. Under the threshold and not warned today: warn Jesse once. Otherwise post nothing and log NO_CHANGE.
